  "passage": {
    "text": "When goods cross a border, they need documents. The most important ones are the invoice and the customs declaration. The invoice shows what the goods are and how much they cost. In the declaration, the company tells customs about the goods. Customs officers check the papers and sometimes they open the boxes. The company often pays a tax. We call this tax duty. If a paper is wrong, the truck must wait at the border. That costs time and money. So a logistics specialist always checks every document twice before the truck leaves.",
